  "“In His Image” is a visual exploration of the idea that our identity is reflected in the beauty, stories and symbols we surround ourselves with. It is a tribute to the human soul as a reflection of the highest Creator.",
  "<strong>Classical fragments</strong>, ancient sculptures and architecture, symbolise shared cultural heritage and the timeless search for perfection and truth. <strong>Living symbols</strong>, butterflies and birds, stand for the soul’s freedom, transformation and the spark of life in every creation. <strong>Layers of identity</strong>: the complex collage shows how our self is assembled from memory, art and the images that inspire us.",
